                    "profile": {
                        "address": "Centennial, Colorado",
                        "reading": "This building at 7059 South Potomac Street in Centennial, Colorado, a Denver suburb in Arapahoe County, is identified in mapping data as a Comcast facility operating under the Xfinity consumer brand. Comcast Corporation, headquartered in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, is one of the largest telecommunications and media companies in the United States, providing cable television, high speed internet, and phone service to residential and business customers across much of the country. Xfinity is the brand name Comcast has used for its cable, internet, and phone services since 2010. A facility of this kind in the Denver metropolitan area would typically support regional network operations for Comcast's Mountain West service territory, housing equipment that manages video, internet, and voice traffic for subscribers in the surrounding region, a function that differs somewhat from a conventional wholesale colocation data center built to lease server space to outside tenants. No source reviewed for this entry states a specific power capacity, square footage, or opening date for this building, and none is estimated here. This entry documents the building's street address and its identification as a Comcast facility while leaving detailed technical specifications unpublished pending better sourcing.",
