                    "country": "US",
                    "profile": {
                        "address": "14312, Northline Road, Southgate, Wayne County, Michigan, 48195",
                        "reading": "Comcast Corporation, the Philadelphia-headquartered telecommunications and media conglomerate, is recorded at a Northline Road location in Southgate, Michigan, a Downriver Detroit suburb in Wayne County along the Interstate 75 corridor south of the city. As is typical for Comcast's network sites, no address confirmation, square footage, power capacity, or facility description specific to this Southgate location is published on the company's own websites or in identifiable local permit or trade-press coverage; Comcast's public materials describe its network investment in the broader Detroit and southeast Michigan market in general terms, covering cable-plant upgrades, expanded gigabit and multi-gig service availability, and periodic local network-expansion announcements, without breaking out individual site addresses, equipment lists, or capacities for the many hub sites, headends, and network facilities that support its Xfinity cable, internet, and voice services across the region.\n\nThat pattern of non-disclosure is standard for the cable and telecommunications industry, and it is informative in itself: unlike a colocation or wholesale data center operator, which sells space and services directly to enterprise tenants and therefore has a commercial incentive to publish specifications that help those tenants evaluate a building, a network operator like Comcast builds and operates a site like this one purely to serve its own subscriber base. There is no outside tenant who needs to know this building's power redundancy or cooling design, and no commercial reason for Comcast to describe it beyond what local franchise and regulatory compliance requires. Facilities of this type in the Comcast network typically function as regional headends or hub sites, points where fiber and coaxial plant serving a metro-area franchise territory converge with the equipment, including encoders, routers, amplifiers, and increasingly virtualized cable-modem termination systems, that originates and manages video and data service to homes and businesses in the surrounding area, rather than as large enterprise or cloud-scale data halls open to outside customers.\n\nSouthgate itself is a small, largely residential and light-industrial Downriver community; it is not a recognized data-center market, and this site's presence there reflects Comcast's need for local network infrastructure serving its Downriver Detroit franchise footprint rather than any broader significance to the region's data-center landscape. No further building-specific detail beyond the general Northline Road location was located in available public sources at the time of writing.",
                        "sources": [
                            {
                                "url": "https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/reverse?lat=42.213902&lon=-83.198214&format=jsonv2",
                                "date": "2026-09-03",
